[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1070,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 1086,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151477,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1086,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma is a benign papillary M&uuml;llerian epithelial tumour that can occur in the vagina or cervix.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1071,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 1087,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151478,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1087,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1072,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1088,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151479,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151480,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> M&uuml;llerian papilloma of infancy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151481,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151482,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papillomas are typically mucosal based but occasionally may be intramural. They occur in the vagina and cervix with relatively similar frequency {26948653}. Vaginal tumours most commonly occur in the upper vagina {26948653}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151483,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases occur in prepubertal girls, with a few reported in adolescents or young adults (age range: 2&ndash;24&nbsp;years) {26948653; 25330952; 21073126; 11737317; 9891250; 14043062}. Most patients present with vaginal bleeding or discharge {26948653}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151484,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are extremely rare vaginal and cervical neoplasms. The predominantly occur in children, with rare adult cases reported {7979569; 26948653; 25330952; 17703455}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151485,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151486,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis is uncertain, but this neoplasm is believed to arise from M&uuml;llerian epithelium {9891250; 6170416}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151487,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucosal-based cases are friable polypoid lesions and measure &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;mm {26948653; 25330952; 19616458}, whereas intramural examples are solid-cystic mural masses {9891250; 6170416}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151488,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histology shows an exophytic or intramural lesion with a papillary architecture and slender fibrovascular cores lined by cuboidal or columnar epithelium, sometimes with a hobnail morphology, with little or no cytological atypia {9891250; 11737317; 19616458}. Nuclei are uniform, with fine chromatin. Mitoses are generally absent or sparse. Squamous metaplasia may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151489,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151490,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151491,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> papillary architecture; cuboidal or columnar epithelium with no cytological atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151492,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign tumours and are not staged.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151493,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 42,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical outcome is favourable, with almost all cases having a benign outcome {26948653; 19616458}, but recurrence, including multiple recurrences, has been reported {30406704; 7979569; 10193336}. Malignant transformation to clear cell carcinoma after multiple recurrences was reported in one vaginal case {12713630}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:19:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]